comments.body:
@andfasano While testing with the OVE installation flow I found we need to add localhost:22625 credentials alongside the api-int entry in the pull secret.

registries.conf on master nodes lists localhost:22625 as a fallback mirror after api-int.<baseDomain>:22625. The fallback is needed during early bootstrap when the api-int VIP is not yet available — keepalived and the load balancer have not fully come up at that stage. Since the IRI registry runs locally on each master, localhost:22625 is reachable even before the VIP is established.

CRI-O looks up credentials by the hostname it actually connects to, so when it falls back to localhost:22625 it cannot find credentials and returns 401. Adding localhost:22625 alongside the api-int entry in the pull secret resolves this.
